c states in the country, having dispatched Seth Moulton in the September primary. Republican John Deaton, running as an anti-Trump, anti-corruption candidate, has struggled to gain traction; even supportive coverage describes his path as difficult.\n\nRecent polls from MassINC and UNH show Markey leading by 22 to 26 points among likely voters, consistent with averages near 24 points. Deaton has raised a credible but modest sum, yet no outside spending has entered on either side. All ten expert ratings call the race Solid or Safe D, and prediction markets price a Markey win at 98 to 99 percent. The race sits firmly in the Safe D category.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9975, "margin": 19.63}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9982, "margin": 20.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9987, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.999, "margin": 24.0}]}